<description>
Swap the visible color of the crossing area between two perpendicular full-span bars.

Input structure:
- The dominant background surrounds two non-background colors.
- One horizontal bar occupies a contiguous band of rows with no background cells.
- One vertical bar occupies a contiguous band of columns with no background cells.
- Their rectangular crossing is uniformly one of the two foreground colors.

Rule:
- Preserve the grid except for the crossing rectangle.
- Recolor every crossing pixel to the other foreground color, making the hidden bar visible there.

Key insight:
- The crossing is exactly the intersection of all-foreground rows and all-foreground columns; its current color identifies the bar on top, so the output flips it to the other bar color.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "two perpendicular full-span foreground bars on the dominant background",
  "transform": "recolor the rectangular crossing of the all-foreground rows and all-foreground columns to the other foreground color; preserve all other pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-13 rows x 6-13 cols, background black (0)
  colors: exactly 2 distinct non-black foreground colors (any from palette)
  horizontal_bar:
    description: contiguous band of rows spanning full grid width, single fg color
    thickness: 1-3 rows
    position: not at row 0 or last row (at least 1 bg row above and below)
  vertical_bar:
    description: contiguous band of columns spanning full grid height, single fg color
    thickness: 1-2 columns
    position: not at col 0 or last col (at least 1 bg col left and right)
  crossing:
    region: rectangle where hbar rows and vbar cols intersect
    color: uniformly one of the two fg colors (the "top" bar's color)
    size: hbar_thickness x vbar_thickness (1-6 cells)
  outside_bars: all cells outside both bars are background (0)
  bars_use_different_colors: hbar color != vbar color [observed]
  transform:
    rule: recolor crossing rectangle to the OTHER fg color (swap top/bottom bar visibility)
    unchanged: all non-crossing cells preserved

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (simple task, no inversion needed)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims H in [6,13], W in [6,13]
    2. Pick 2 distinct non-zero colors c_h, c_v
    3. Pick hbar thickness t_h in [1,3] and starting row r in [1, H-t_h-1]
    4. Pick vbar thickness t_v in [1,2] and starting col c in [1, W-t_v-1]
    5. Fill grid with 0; paint hbar rows [r, r+t_h) across all cols with c_h
    6. Paint vbar cols [c, c+t_v) across all rows with c_v
    7. Pick which bar is "on top" (50/50); fill crossing with that bar's color
